WEBVTT

00:02:28.836 --> 00:02:30.156
That's just frightening."

00:02:30.156 --> 00:02:33.716
Take that 11 kilometers
and turn it on its side.

00:02:35.076 --> 00:02:38.636
I reckon most people in the room
have traveled 11 kilometers today.

00:02:39.116 --> 00:02:42.836
And the other thing
that we don't like is the unknown.

00:02:42.876 --> 00:02:45.436
And this is where we get
into this whole relationship

00:02:45.476 --> 00:02:48.636
between reality
and what we're told on the TV.

00:02:49.196 --> 00:02:51.156
So on the TV, we're quite regularly told

00:02:51.156 --> 00:02:53.436
that we know more
about the surface of the Moon

00:02:53.436 --> 00:02:55.116
than we know about the deep sea.

00:02:55.116 --> 00:02:59.436
For starters, that quote goes back
before the Apollo missions

00:02:59.436 --> 00:03:03.276
and a time where we knew not very much
about the Moon or the deep sea.